# Tutorials: each story is one page that walks the reader through the flight computer, step by
# step. The rules that no story shows are tested on their own.

Story: Checking the sticks on the serial line
  As a pilot with a TX15
  I want to see that each stick reaches ArduPilot
  So that I know the plane does what my hands do

  Before the first flight with the flight computer, move each stick and switch, and look at the
  channels that ArduPilot reads. A centred stick is 1500 us. The ends of a stick are 1000 us
  and 2000 us.

  Scenario: Centre, full travel, half travel, arm
    When 5 seconds pass
    Then the roll channel is 1500 us
    And the pitch channel is 1500 us
    When the TX15 roll stick is 100 %
    And the TX15 throttle stick is 100 %
    And 5 seconds pass
    Then the roll channel is at least 1990 us
    And the throttle channel is at least 1990 us
    When the TX15 pitch stick is -50 %
    And 5 seconds pass
    Then the pitch channel is at least 1245 us
    And the pitch channel is at most 1255 us
    When the TX15 arm switch is on
    And 5 seconds pass
    Then the arm channel is at least 1900 us

Story: Losing the TX15 and getting it back
  As a pilot with a TX15
  I want the plane to fail safe when the line goes quiet
  So that a lost link does not leave the throttle open

  You unplug the TX15 while the throttle is at half. The flight computer sets the throttle
  below the failsafe level of ArduPilot. You plug the TX15 in, and the throttle comes back.

  Scenario: Unplug, then plug in again
    When the TX15 throttle stick is 50 %
    When the TX15 is not connected
    And 5 seconds pass
    Then the throttle channel is at most 900 us
    And the TX15 uplink quality is 0 %
    When the TX15 is connected
    And 5 seconds pass
    Then the throttle channel is at least 1490 us
    And the TX15 uplink quality is 100 %

Story: Commanding the plane from the ground station
  As a pilot with a TX15
  I want the ground station to see and command the plane through the TX15
  So that it needs no radio of its own

  The ground station gets the telemetry of ArduPilot through the TX15. You fly the plane away
  from home, and the map follows it. You send a command, and it goes up the same line. When you
  unplug the TX15, the ground station hears nothing.

  Scenario: Hear the plane, follow it, command it, lose it
    When the ground station telemetry is flowing
    And 5 seconds pass
    Then the ground station telemetry is flowing
    When the ground station map distance is 400 m
    And 5 seconds pass
    Then the ground station map distance is 400 m
    When the ground station command is sent
    And 5 seconds pass
    Then the autopilot command is received
    When 10 seconds pass
    Then the ground station telemetry rate is at most 4000 bytes per second
    When the TX15 is not connected
    And 10 seconds pass
    Then the ground station telemetry is silent

Story: Reading the flight display
  As a pilot with a TX15
  I want the screen of the TX15 to show the flight as a flight display
  So that I see the mode, the attitude, the speeds, the battery and what ArduPilot says

  You follow a short flight on the screen of the TX15. First, a PreArm check fails. Then the
  plane arms, flies, banks, and comes home in RTL with a low battery. Each step changes one
  reading on the screen.

  Scenario: From PreArm to RTL
    When the TX15 screen message is PreArm: Throttle (RC3) is not neutral
    And 5 seconds pass
    Then the TX15 screen message is PreArm: Throttle (RC3) is not neutral
    When the TX15 screen arming is armed
    And 5 seconds pass
    Then the TX15 screen arming is armed
    When the TX15 screen satellites is 9
    And 5 seconds pass
    Then the TX15 screen satellites is 9
    When the TX15 screen airspeed is 18 m/s
    And 5 seconds pass
    Then the TX15 screen airspeed is 18 m/s
    When the TX15 screen bank is 30 degrees
    And 5 seconds pass
    Then the TX15 screen bank is 30 degrees
    When the TX15 screen mode is RTL
    And the TX15 screen climb is -3 m/s
    And 5 seconds pass
    Then the TX15 screen mode is RTL
    And the TX15 screen climb is -3 m/s
    When the TX15 screen battery is 11.1 V
    And 5 seconds pass
    Then the TX15 screen battery is 11.1 V
